		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: calculating new object location]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=30549#p30549"><![CDATA[
You're absolutely right. At first I wanted to choose a partial solution, which I thought would make my life easier. I was wrong. It's partial and harder to implement.<br><br>What I had before I started this thread was:<br>1. Server sends world information to client<br>2. Client sets state according to message &lt;-- this is where objects in client world jumps from place to place<br>3. Client sends state to server<br><br>I wanted to just update the controlling character's position based on the deltaT, meaning to calculate new position, move while performing collision detection. As I said, this is both partial and hard to implement.<br>Instead, what I'm doing now, which is super easy to implement, is to keep track of the time between deltas and call something like this:<div class="codebox"><p>Code: </p><pre><code>StepPhysics( m_ConnectStart.GetDelta() - m_LastDeltaTicks );</code></pre></div>Easier, proven, and works for all objects.<br><br>Thanks for the advice buddy!<br>Mike<br><br>P.S: thanks for taking the time to read the article. I think it's great, I hope you enjoyed it as much as I did.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=9290">mike1</a> — Mon Apr 22, 2013 2:23 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
