Hi Jyavoc,<br>Thanks for the reply!<br>You can read more about games networking in this article: <a href="http://gafferongames.com/networking-for-game-programmers/what-every-programmer-needs-to-know-about-game-networking/" class="postlink">http://gafferongames.com/networking-for ... etworking/</a><br>I do something very similar to what you suggested - the client &amp; server decide on their own 'epoc' time and every delta has the milliseconds since then.<br><br>However, my question isn't about how to make a network game, but more detailed and technical: what Bullet APIs should I use to calculate an object's new location, given its speed and time passed.<br>Ideally I would like a function that looks like this:<div class="codebox"><p>Code: </p><pre><code>void MoveObject(object, previousTransform, velocity, angularVelocity, deltaT);</code></pre></div>And this function would take into consideration collisions, etc.<br><br>Any idea how to implement such a function?<br><br>Thanks,<br>Mike<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=9290">mike1</a> — Fri Apr 19, 2013 2:15 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
